# Korean typography (portfolio)

## Line breaks

- CSS must keep `:lang(ko) { word-break: keep-all; }` on body copy — never split syllables mid-word (실|물, 됩니|다).
- `.key-concept` highlights use `word-break: keep-all` so marked phrases stay intact.
- Set `document.documentElement.lang` when locale changes (already in `applyLanguage()`).

## i18n `**highlight**` markers

- Put Korean particles **inside** the highlight, not after:
  - Bad: `**실물 하이파이브**를` → Good: `**실물 하이파이브를**`
  - Bad: `**팀 프로젝트**를` → Good: `**팀 프로젝트를**`
- Avoid `을(를)` parenthetical josa — restructure or use `es-hangul` `josa()`.

## Verification

```zsh
cd portfolio && npm run lint:ko && node scripts/test-korean-linebreak.mjs
```

`lint-korean-copy.mjs` flags orphan particles after `**` and missing CSS `keep-all`.
